      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2013 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Dialysis vascular access associated coronary-subclavian steal or hypoperfusion syndrome is an uncommon but potentially life threatening condition. Awareness of this syndrome is important in the management of vascular access in hemodialysis patients. We report a case of dialysis vascular access associated coronary-subclavian steal syndrome and review the literature on its pathogenesis and therapeutic implications."
      },
